# TI-59/PC-100A Program: Calendar Printer, by Bill Skillman
#
# From 52-Notes, V3N6p2. This is a series of calendar programs that started
# with issue V3N5 of 52-Notes. This issue contained three programs, and later
# editions kept adding faster and more compact programs. Our goal is to collect
# and preserve them here in the form of preload files.
#
# This is the documentation given for this program in the original article:
#
# Bill Skillman worked out a simpler way to pack print buffers for all
# cases from a block of consecutive registers, each containing print-code
# for a single day. His approach is the fastest yet: 73 minutes per year.
# The program which follows is a revision of Bill's, cutting size and
# execution time a bit with the substitution of INV Dszs for x-t
# comparisons, and a bunch of equally spaced GTOs for a double indirect
# mechanization (the latter being more costly in registers, and slightly
# slower, even though more elegant).
#
# User Instructions:
# 1. Key start year, press A.
# 2. Key start month, press R/S; if wrong module, display flashes.
#    For 1 Month: Press B; for balance of year, press C; for specified
#    interval, key end year, press D.

MODEL: TI-59
SOLID-STATE-MODULE: ML
PRINTER: on

CUECARD:
Template: MagnetCard
Title: Calendar Printer
Banks: 1,3
A: START YEAR
B: 1 MONTH
C: TO YR END
D: END YEAR

